rd along with the movie  references there of course plenty of  references to Batman mythology Arthur's  social worker is named Deborah Kane  Deborah Kane is also a social worker in  the comic Batman the ultimate evil  the name Kane pops up throughout the  Batman stories and is actually derived  from Bob Kane who co-created the  character of Batman in one shot we see  Fleck running down a hallway with a  folder this is likely Arkham  which we saw sign for in the first  teaser Thomas Wayne Bruce Wayne's father  also pops up just a joke to you in the  same shot Wayne appears dressed up in a  tuxedo could this be the fateful night  when Bruce Wayne's parents are murdered  the Joker is the one who kills Wayne's  parents in the 1989 version of Batman  but non 2005's Batman Begins or in the  comics however at one point in the  trailer you can see a newspaper front  page with a drawing of a clown Paris a  headline that reads latest news on the  murders is it referring to a potential  string of murders or the murders of  Thomas and Martha Wayne and to top that  all off there's a brief glimpse outside  the monarch theatre the theatre in which  the Williams attended show before their  murder the trailer also gives us some  deeper glimpses at the movie's plot  including that at one point Joker's  mother penny Fleck will end up in the  hospital for reasons still unknown we  also get more shots of the Joker's  growing cult following we see somebody  holding a sign that shaped like the  clown mask that Joker's followers wear  the violence we see suggests that this  could be a full-on rebellion you can  also spot a massive clown head here in  the background that looks similar to the  masks we also see him walk by this image  which is a real 1873 painting of the  lion tamer and it wouldn't be the Joker  without his iconic laughs which we hear  again a few times in this final trailer  was there anything we missed  let us know in the comments  [Music]
 

